    "observed_at": "2026-11-11T17:02:10.460895-05:00",
    "finding": "Raw FPGA display uses sm_env_dump_0/1 sysfs callbacks, each returning 4096 bytes. Kernel reports bad count for both callbacks and its read layer. Two concatenated reads yield 8190 bytes.",
    "inference": "Consistent with Linux 5.15 sysfs clamping each PAGE_SIZE return to PAGE_SIZE-1. Do not interpret the concatenation as contiguous 8192-byte memory: the last byte of each 4096-byte block is omitted.",
    "impact": "All currently decoded fan fields and independent anchors lie in the first chunk, so their positions are unaffected. Warning is a diagnostic callback issue, not proven cooling failure. Further raw polling stopped; normal environmental CLI used.",
